  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "moderate",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present risk is dominated by a TC1 path from untrusted public issues to broad private-repository reads and attacker-readable public PR creation. The only declared preventive control on that path is a per-tool approval prompt that operates as a model-summary gate because arguments are collapsed and approvals are frequent, so rubric step 2 reduces critical inherent risk to a moderate residual floor. Forecast returns to critical if that gate decays under model upgrade, approval fatigue, autonomy increase, or removal. A secondary present risk is MCP supply-chain tampering because definitions are unpinned and peer identity is not verified."
  },
